      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Charge-migration (inductive, 'i') cleavage of the same C4-C5 bond, but with the charge retained on the alkyl fragment: gives the n-butyl cation C4H9+ (m/z 57, 10%) plus the neutral acetyl radical CH3-C(.)=O. Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: Eq. 8.2 is a thermochemical fragmentation map (log k printed above each reaction arrow, heats of formation printed below each species), not a curved-arrow figure. All electron moves here are curator-inferred from the mechanism-type label printed under the reaction arrow; none is drawn on the page. Encoded as TWO fishhooks that split the C4-C5 sigma pair heterolytically toward the carbonyl: move<1> one electron onto C5 (the new acyl radical site), move<2> the other electron onto O6 where it pairs with the pre-existing odd electron (quenching the O radical and neutralising O+); C4 is thereby left electron-deficient as the butyl cation."
